# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Atlas "Connect" URI has an EMPTY path after the host — see the `/` right
# before `?appName=`. MongoDB then has no default database to select, and the
# driver falls back to one literally named `test`. That is a real hazard, not a
# cosmetic one: the application will boot, `/api/health` will answer `healthy`,
# and every collection will be created in a database nobody named.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@decoricks-cluster0.q4qnwaa.mongodb.net/?appName=Decoricks-Cluster0

# The database this application's records live in. Set it explicitly rather than
# relying on the URI path or the driver fallback; `scripts/db-inventory.ts` prints
# the current effective database and its row counts if you are unsure.
# Resolution order: MONGODB_TEST_DB > MONGODB_DB > MONGODB_URI path > driver
# default (which logs a warning on boot). Never point this at a database that
# holds another project's data.
MONGODB_DB=<decoricks or the database that actually holds this app's records>

# Test databases only. Honoured ONLY under NODE_ENV=test (Vitest) or when
# E2E_TEST_MODE=1 (the Playwright webServer sets this automatically) —
# src/lib/db-name.ts refuses to honour this variable otherwise, so a stray
# value in .env.local cannot redirect production traffic at the test DB.
# It always wins over MONGODB_DB, so a test run cannot be aimed at production.
MONGODB_TEST_DB=decoricks_test

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sessions (replaces NextAuth)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs CSRF tokens. Minimum 16 characters.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-32-random-bytes

# Minutes of inactivity before a session expires. Defaults to 7 days; the
# window restarts on each qualifying (non-background) authenticated request.
SESSION_TTL_MINUTES=10080
# Minimum seconds between session slides, so bursts of requests do not cause
# bursts of writes. Auto-polling requests never slide.
SESSION_SLIDE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password policy
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH=12
BCRYPT_COST=12

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Login lockout
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOGIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
LOGIN_WINDOW_MINUTES=15
LOCKOUT_MINUTES=15

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# First Founder (used only by `npm run seed`)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The seed refuses to run against MONGODB_TEST_DB and will not overwrite an
# existing Founder's credentials on rerun.
FOUNDER_EMAIL=founder@decoricks.pk
FOUNDER_NAME=Abdullah
FOUNDER_PASSWORD=<at least 12 chars, upper+lower+number>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web Push (Phase 9, OPTIONAL)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When missing, push notifications are disabled and the app falls back to
# in-app + browser notifications while open. These values are server-only.
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=replace-with-your-vapid-private-key
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:your-email@example.com

# The one VAPID value the browser needs, for `PushManager.subscribe()`.
# MISSING THIS IS THE COMMON FAILURE: with only the two server keys set, push
# stays silently disabled — `notifications/push.ts` requires all three.
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is inlined into the client at BUILD time on Netlify/Vercel, so
# it must be present in the build environment, not only in the runtime one, and
# changing it needs a rebuild rather than a re-deploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=replace-with-your-vapid-public-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Process clock (REQUIRED in practice on a serverless host)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole date layer assumes a process clock NAMED Asia/Karachi: it renders
# Karachi wall time and re-parses it in the process zone, so an equivalent offset
# under another name (Asia/Lahore, also +05:00) shifts every stored timestamp by
# five hours exactly as UTC does. Measured in Phase 5 §7: 0.000h on
# Asia/Karachi, +5.000h on UTC, +5.000h on Asia/Lahore.
#
# `src/instrumentation.node.ts` sets this for you when TZ is UNSET, and warns on
# every boot when the running clock is not Karachi — it never overrides an
# explicit value, because the test suite deliberately runs under TZ=UTC.
# Netlify gives every container a UTC clock: leave TZ unset to take the pin, or
# set it to exactly this value. Do not set it to UTC.
# TZ=Asia/Karachi
